---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About" description="Kieran Ryan makes porcelain and crystalline-glazed ceramics on the East End of New York.">
  <section class="container grid piece-head">
    <p class="label">(About)</p>
    <h1 class="heading">Glaze chemistry, slow cooling, and a little luck</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-label="Bio">
    <div class="grid split">
      <p class="label">(Bio)</p>
      <div class="content prose">
        <p>
          I'm a ceramic artist on the East End of New York. Most of my work is porcelain finished in
          crystalline glaze, a process where zinc and silica crystals grow across the surface while
          the kiln cools. The chemistry and the firing schedule set the conditions. The crystals
          decide the rest, which is why no two pieces match.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also slip cast and 3D print in clay, and I teach crystalline glaze workshops at the
          Clay Art Guild of the Hamptons and classes at Mudita Ceramics School. My work has been
          shown at the Parrish Art Museum.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
    <div class="grid split">
      <h2 class="label" id="process-heading">(Process)</h2>
      <ol class="content steps">
        <li>
          <span class="n">1</span>
          <h3>Form</h3>
          <p>Each piece is thrown, slip cast in a plaster mold, or printed layer by layer in clay.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="n">2</span>
          <h3>Glaze</h3>
          <p>Glazes are mixed by hand from raw materials, with zinc and silica as the crystal builders.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="n">3</span>
          <h3>Fire</h3>
          <p>The kiln holds at set temperatures on the way down, and that's where the crystals grow.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
